1] Find all employees with name having L at 3rd position and E at second last position.

==> select * from emp where name regexp'^..L.*E.$';

2] Find all employees with name not starting with A or M
==> select * from emp where regexp_like (ename , '^[^AM]');

3] Display all employees with sal >1000 and sal<3000 and job has A at starting position and ends with T.
==> select * from emp where sal>1000 and sal<=3000 and regexp_like (job,'^A .* T$');

4] Write a query  to display empno, ename, sal, commission, increased sal by 10% and for all employees  whose  name starts with A,M or S.

==> select empno , ename , sal, comm,sal*1.10 from emp where regexp_like(ename,'^[AMS]');

